=== and the other direction: no arm of disposition_of names a class class_or_fail does not.
=== A dead arm is invisible to the listing above, and it is how a class removed from the log
=== taxonomy would leave a disposition behind that nothing can ever ask for.
  the two lists are the same, in both directions

=== the one arm that reads the carries: a bounded choice the session enumerated
with options:    AI-resolvable
one option:      AI-resolvable
a lone string, which a session may still write where the contract says a list:
                 AI-resolvable
=== and the shapes a session writes when it had none, which must not look bounded
empty options:   human-required
empty string:    human-required
an object:       human-required
the number nil:  human-required
no options:      human-required
no carries:      human-required
carries not json:human-required

=== a class neither list holds is refused, not defaulted
exit 1
exit 1

=== a disposition is not a class, and asking the wrong question fails where it is visible
exit 2
